  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Fill in the missing values in the truth table below.\n\n| ${x}_{1}$ | ${x}_{2}$ | $¬{x}_{2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $0$ | $1$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $1$ | $0$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $1$ | $1$ | {{field-4}} |",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that $\\text{True}=1$ and $\\text{False}=0.$ \n\nAlso, the negation $¬{x}_{2}$ is true if and only if ${x}_{2}$ is false ($0$).\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Boolean function is the following: \n\n| ${x}_{1}$ | ${x}_{2}$ | $¬{x}_{2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| $1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $0$ |",
